<title>INDIA: Good demand improves Indian soybean prices.</title>
<headline>Good demand improves Indian soybean prices.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were firm in central Indian markets on good demand from processsing plants, dealers said on Friday.</p>
<p>Prices were up by 300-400 rupees per tonne and arrivals were around 1,200 tonnes in central markets today. Business volumes were good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also firm with soyoil solvent up by 300 rupees and soyoil refined up by 200 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady in thin trade as export demand was dull against poor supply from Indian processors and exporters. Soymeal yellow was $307-308 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for exports. Rapeseed extraction was $115 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 3,900-3,950 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. The undertone was steady.</p>
